omen
====

omen is a bounty-oriented hybrid scanner for Ethereum trace vulnerabilities.
It stands on the shoulders of prior art and open-source libraries listed below.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prior art
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MAIAN
-----
The prodigal / suicidal / greedy taxonomy of trace vulnerabilities, and the
hybrid symbolic-analysis-plus-concrete-validation approach, originate from:

    Ivica Nikolic, Aashish Kolluri, Ilya Sergey, Prateek Saxena, and Aquinas
    Hobor. "Finding The Greedy, Prodigal, and Suicidal Contracts at Scale."
    Proceedings of the 34th Annual Computer Security Applications Conference
    (ACSAC 2018). (Also presented in the USENIX Security community context,
    2018.)

    Reference implementation: https://github.com/ivicanikolicsg/MAIAN

omen reframes that taxonomy for modern EVM tooling and a web3-bounty workflow.
omen does NOT reuse MAIAN's source code; it reimplements the detection on top
of a modern, maintained analysis engine (Slither).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Libraries
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Slither (slither-analyzer)
--------------------------
omen's source-mode detection is built on the Slither static analysis
framework and its detector primitives.

    Slither — https://github.com/crytic/slither
    Copyright (c) Crytic / Trail of Bits
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0).

omen invokes Slither as a library dependency. Users redistributing omen
together with Slither must comply with Slither's AGPL-3.0 terms.

Other dependencies (each under its own license):
    pyevmasm   — EVM (dis)assembler (Trail of Bits)
    web3.py    — Ethereum JSON-RPC client
    eth-abi    — Ethereum ABI encoding/decoding
    eth-utils, eth-typing — Ethereum Python utilities

See each project's repository for full license text.
